<title>TURKEY: Cukurova Elektrik 96 net profits soar.</title>
<headline>Cukurova Elektrik 96 net profits soar.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     10,893.28 vs   1,076.82</p>
<p>    Net profit			 5,446.64 vs     538.41</p>
<p>    Net sales			 29,264.19 vs  13,411.39</p>
<p>    Operating profit		10,935.36 vs   3,983.13</p>
<p>    Exceptional income		 860.73 vs     969.17</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		674.05 vs   1,578.44</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    4,148.82 vs   2,614.82</p>
<p>    Total debts		     23,968.17 vs  15,619.01</p>
<p>    Equity			     7,487.94 vs   2,678.04</p>
<p>    Capital				500.00 vs     500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's biggest private sector utility Cukurova Elektrik A.S. produces and distributes power in southern Cukurova region. Its major shareholder is the Rumeli group run by the Uzan family.</p>
<p>Figures do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
